WEBVTT

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.650
Chirp, chirp, chirp. Chirpity-chirp.

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.740
Good morning!

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.990
Looks like you overslept again, huh?

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.500
Did you get enough sleep?

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:12.250
Yeah.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:13.880
I'm...

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.810
Suzuki-san, good morning.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:17.810
I...

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.140
Good morning, Yushi-kun!

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.610
Good morning!

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.320
I'm really back!

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:28.820
Good morning!

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:33.630
Tempura soba! And such pretty temari sushi!

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:39.730
And the sauce for
the ankake soba is just perfect!

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:42.910
The squid and spring vegetable
tempura is good, too!

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.140
It's nice and crispy!

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:49.530
Da...

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:51.280
Da...

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:52.940
Da...

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:54.510
Da?

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:56.660
Da smell of dashi broth!

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.570
Soba! Sushi! Japanese food!

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.200
Oh, Furuhonya-san! Welcome back.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:41.930
<b>Sixth Haunting
Petit Hierozoicon</b>

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.540
It's so good!

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:42.340
I love it!

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.760
Furuhonya-san lives here.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.140
He hasn't been back for a year or so, though.

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:52.390
You're the best, Ruriko-chan! The best!

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:54.890
You really are the best chef!

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:57.650
How I've missed you this past year and a half!

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:00.230
This rice, these pickled vegetables,
they're the best!

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:03.730
But where have you been that 
you ended up like that?

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.060
He's ready to drink already.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.900
I've been journeying from 
Africa to the Middle East.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.610
And all over the countryside, too.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.910
There wasn't even anything 
I could stand to eat,

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.520
let alone Japanese food.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:17.260
Furuhonya, do you sell old books?

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:18.280
That's right.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:21.470
I was looking for a book of 
spells called <i>The Black Mary</i>

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:25.640
that's a mix of early Christianity 
and African folk religion.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.340
I never did find it, though.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.310
I see...

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:32.270
But I did find a lot of interesting stuff,

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.770
like the Dead Sea Scrolls, 
<i>The Book of Adventures</i>,

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:36.810
and <i>The Book of the Multiverse</i>.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:41.040
Those are all extremely 
famous magical books...

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.440
I don't know if I believe they exist.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:46.940
Well, they're things you could 
never get via normal methods!

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.120
Another shady guy...

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:55.040
I do love Japanese tea.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.100
So who are you?

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.290
So late!

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:01.460
Oh, you're new here, huh?

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:03.010
Sorry, sorry.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.480
Yushi-kun loves books, too.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.010
I bet you'll get along, huh?

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.890
Right...

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.630
Want to see?

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.180
Amazing, right?

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:19.350
For example, the Voynich manuscript. 
One of the rarest books of them all.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.340
In the year 1912,

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:26.030
a bookseller named Voynich found a manuscript 
in a certain temple and copied it into this.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:30.450
It's said that Roger Bacon wrote the 
manuscript in the 13th century,

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.870
but it contains drawings of sunflowers,

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:36.080
which should have only become known 
to Europe in the 15th century,

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:39.890
illustrations of sperm and ovum, 
concepts which didn't even exist yet,

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:43.420
as well as a drawing of 
the Andromeda Galaxy!

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.480
Well? Amazing, huh?

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:48.610
It's the original <i>Venus in Furs</i>!

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:51.280
You've got <i>The 120 Days of Sodom</i>, too!

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:54.480
Hey, if you're not buying,
then put them back!

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.090
I think there's a limit to how many 
books you can fit in a trunk.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:04:59.900
Is there some kind of trick to it?

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:12.530
That feels strange.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:14.070
Did something unusual get mixed in with them?

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:15.480
Strange?

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.960
It's easy for people's emotions 
to gather in books.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.500
They're collections of words with will.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.460
Especially magic books.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:26.260
And used books are ones
 that were, well, used, so...

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:32.340
This is it!

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:36.450
What's this, Furuhonya-san?

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:38.690
Hmm, what was that again?

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:41.810
Somebody at a flea market gave 
it to me for free as a bonus.

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:44.140
It didn't feel dangerous.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:51.300
Is it an artbook of tarot cards?

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:53.220
The names are weird, right?

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:57.610
For instance, card 1 in
tarot is the Magician, right?

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:00.360
This picture is the Magician,

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:03.790
but I can't read the name on the card.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:05.050
What is that?

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:07.230
A code? Ancient script?

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:10.290
I've never seen it, either.

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:13.760
Furuhonya-san, this book is probably...

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:16.190
Sealed.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:17.530
Sealed?

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:22.780
It has some power, but that power has 
been locked away so it can't be used.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:25.250
That's why we can't read 
the names of the pictures.

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:27.140
So I got lucky, huh?

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:28.810
A real magic book!

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:30.630
A magic book?

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:31.990
Thanks, Akine-chan.

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:34.200
I owe your sensors big time!

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.060
What will you do with it?

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:39.070
Books like this can be tricky to handle,

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:41.990
but collectors will pay a ton for them.

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:44.030
<i>I should've figured.</i>

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:46.080
Yup.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:50.370
So I'll see if it's safe for you.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:53.720
I'll have master take a look at it before 
I tell you if it's safe to sell.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:55.670
What? No...

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:57.760
You don't want to have to deal 
with some weird power, right?

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.950
A magic book, huh?

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:01.430
So they really exist.

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:03.570
Okay, I'm off to work!

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:07.230
In England, parapsychology is 
a recognized field of study.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:10.560
Not only is "magician" a real job there,

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.100
but it has its own status.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:14.880
So sometimes it's actually harder 
to have things printed there,

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:17.410
and so they're brought
to Japan or published here.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:21.020
This book, written by a real 
man named Aleister Crowley,

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:22.340
is one example.

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:24.680
But still, there were all 
kinds of problems with it,

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:27.050
and it caused a big fuss.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.210
Reimei-san, you know what I mean, right?

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:32.380
You deal with words for a living.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:33.970
That's right.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:38.390
Sometimes I put words down on a page and 
they turn into something different.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:39.480
Something different?

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:42.810
The printed word is a tricky thing.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.050
More than images or sculptures.

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:48.320
For example, the <i>Venus de Milo</i>.

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.530
Some people say that if 
it had both its arms,

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.540
it wouldn't be as famous as it is today.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:08:00.670
That's because your imagination can fill in
what the missing arms might have looked like.

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:05.530
The printed word gives you the biggest
opportunity to use your imagination, right?

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:09.460
That's where we get the word 
"kotodama," or a word of power.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.710
<i>That's right.</i>

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.590
<i>When I wasn't fitting 
in at my uncle's house,</i>

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.300
<i>my one source of entertainment was words.</i>

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:21.320
<i>They could take me anywhere.</i>

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.060
<i>I could be anyone.</i>

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:27.520
There are probably a lot of people who see

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:31.110
the demon-summoning rituals in 
this book and actually try them.

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:37.130
Maybe some of them even succeed.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.710
That's what makes books scary.

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:44.360
They become a catalyst to amplify 
humanity's latent abilities.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:49.040
<i>Is that what Akine-chan meant by 
emotions building up in them?</i>

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:58.720
Let's drink!

00:08:58.720 --> 00:08:59.960
These people...

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:04.450
Well, magic books have 
nothing to do with me.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.420
This is paradise.

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:16.780
This apartment is the best!

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:18.820
Yeah, I missed it, too.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:20.450
I was gone for six months.

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:23.860
Why did you come back?

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:26.760
Because...

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:30.170
I was lonely.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:34.800
No, what am I saying?

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:41.620
It's fun here, ain't it?

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:43.460
Yeah!

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.690
Hey, what are you talking about?

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:48.710
Let me join!

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.050
Mariko-san, this is the men's bath!

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:54.290
This one's bigger, though!

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:58.650
Mariko-chan hasn't changed a bit huh?

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:00.790
That was a little too much fanservice.

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:04.540
She's a ghost. She's not 
supposed to be that visible.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:07.650
Ryu-san doesn't mind.

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:10.840
She's not actually physically there, though.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:11.920
That's what he said.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.290
Wow.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:15.360
Okay, night!

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:19.680
<i>I'm tired.</i>

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:24.430
<i>What a long day.</i>

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:26.090
<i>But...</i>

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:28.730
<i>I feel good.</i>

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.750
<i>I'm going to hang out with Hase tomorrow.</i>

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:35.790
<i>He'll be happy I came back.</i>

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:38.710
<i>Someday, I want to invite him here.</i>

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:40.960
<i>What will he think?</i>

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:43.210
<i>Of course, he'll be surprised.</i>

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:45.600
<i>But I'm sure...</i>

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:04.900
Good evening.

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:10.340
Huh?

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:12.600
I thought I was asleep.

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:22.290
It's an honor to meet you, master.

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:35.630
My name is Fool.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.450
It's a pleasure to meet you!

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:43.480
After such a long long journey, 
we have finally met a master,

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:45.000
and we are so very happy!

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:48.560
I hope this is the start of a long—
don't go to sleep, master!

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:51.810
Quiet. I'm tired.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:54.640
If you want to play, go visit someone else!

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:55.730
Wait!

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:59.020
This is the time of day 
when your channel opened!

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:01.790
Please, listen to me, master!

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:05.020
Who's your master?

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:07.180
You are, Yushi-sama.

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:12.240
I see.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.080
This is a dream, huh?

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:16.460
I guess that's okay, then.

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:18.080
Sure thing.

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:19.930
Let's hear you out.

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:21.890
Thank you.

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:23.900
First, behold!

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:29.430
This is the book of tarot card 
drawings that Furuhonya had, right?

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:30.150
Indeed!

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:33.100
This is me.

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:35.780
Yeah, it does say "Fool."

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.770
I can read the names of the cards now.

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:40.940
Wh-What?

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:43.410
Congratulations!

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:47.680
The seal on the book has now 
been successfully broken.

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:52.490
You have indeed been 
recognized as our master.

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:54.810
The seal was broken?

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:58.700
There is a great book of magic in 
this world called the <i>Hierozoicon</i>.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:01.820
It contains 78 monsters that a great mage

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:04.800
summoned from another dimension 
and sealed within.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:09.260
Its master can summon them 
at will and control them.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:12.350
And this is a lesser version of it.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:16.220
A magical book which contains 22 monsters.

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:19.450
The <i>Petit Hierozoicon</i>!

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:21.780
The <i>Petit Hierozoicon</i>, huh?

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:23.310
I see.

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:28.340
Twenty-two means that they're modeled
after the tarot's Major Arcana.

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:30.780
So this is a parody
in two senses of the word.

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:34.360
The creator of this book 
has left this world.

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:38.620
He sealed us away until 
our next master appeared.

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:43.550
For many years, we passed 
from one hand to the next.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.920
But at last, we have found you!

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:49.120
Our new master, Inaba Yushi-sama!

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:51.000
Give us any order you like.

00:13:51.590 --> 00:13:53.070
Order?

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:55.170
But I'm just a high school student.

00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:56.830
Wait, this is stupid.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:58.160
This is just a dream.

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:00.360
Why take it seriously?

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:05.700
Fool, you're basically 
like Ryu-san's familiars?

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:09.170
Indeed, we are similar.

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:12.440
By the way, I am Niyurius,
or number 0, Fool.

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:13.890
Your guide to this book,

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:17.460
and the negotiator between 
you and the monsters.

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:18.650
I see.

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:20.910
So what I don't know I ask you, right?

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:22.830
Yes, anything.

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:25.240
Okay, I'll try it.

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.250
Jin, the Magician!

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:30.900
Jin!

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:35.220
The omnipotent spirit!
Like the genie in Aladdin's lamp!

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:36.970
Aladdin?

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:39.640
The one who grants any wish?

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:45.230
W-Wow!

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:47.980
Give him any order you like, master.

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:53.040
We exist to fulfill your wishes.

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:55.990
Um... um...

00:14:57.650 --> 00:15:00.690
Okay. Money!

00:15:00.690 --> 00:15:02.670
Money you can use in Japan!

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:20.080
That's all?

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:22.100
We are petit, after all,

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:24.080
so Jin lacks stamina.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.810
You can't use him for a while.

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:28.290
Master?

00:15:28.930 --> 00:15:31.180
Okay, I'll try this one next.

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:32.870
High Priestess Sylph!

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:34.000
Sylph!

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:35.860
The spirit of the wind!

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:45.670
I guess I'll try the Hermit next.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.610
Chokmah!

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:51.960
A clan of gods of knowledge,
who serve Minerva, the goddess of wisdom!

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:54.300
He knows all the wisdom of this world!

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.080
Old man, wake up!

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:03.720
We have a new master to serve!

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:06.540
Are you serving dinner now?

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:08.360
You already ate!

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:09.830
Snap out of it!

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:12.420
I'm hungry.

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:14.770
You always forget so quickly.

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:16.820
S'okay, old man. Go back.

00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:22.610
The guy who made this was 
quite the prankster, huh?

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:24.700
Aw, you're flattering me.

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:25.850
Nope.

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:29.280
I guess this'll be the last one.

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:30.980
The Hanged Man.

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:31.830
Cait Sith.

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:35.500
Cait Sith!

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:36.760
A clan of cat kings!

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.460
Known for wearing boots!

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.570
He's so unmotivated.

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:48.420
It's gonna rain tomorrow.

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:52.180
A girl will reject you tomorrow.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:56.170
Cait Sith, how can you talk 
to our master like that?!

00:16:56.150 --> 00:16:57.690
Okay, it's my bedtime.

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:59.110
You can't talk like that!

00:16:57.690 --> 00:16:59.110
Talk to you tomorrow.

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:01.500
Understood!

00:17:05.140 --> 00:17:07.370
That's creepy.

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:09.840
I had the weirdest dream last night.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.070
Stop it.

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:13.400
Why are you talking about dreams?

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:14.870
Don't say that.

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:17.350
It's a pretty neat story.

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:18.620
That stuff's boring.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:21.150
The real world's way more interesting.

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:22.410
But...

00:17:24.610 --> 00:17:26.010
Idiot!

00:17:26.390 --> 00:17:28.380
Screw you, jerk!

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:30.480
Come on, we placed our order!

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:36.440
B-But the fountain drinks are only available 
to customers who ordered from them...

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:40.000
Any proof we shared drinks?

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:43.910
Also, this is the non-smoking section...

00:17:44.170 --> 00:17:48.290
Jeez, you find people like that everywhere.

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:49.410
This place is crap.

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:50.220
Let's leave.

00:17:50.220 --> 00:17:51.750
We're customers!

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:53.390
I guess we should leave, too.

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:54.540
It spoiled the meal.

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:56.320
Yeah.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:58.590
<b>Total</b>

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:58.590
Thank you!

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:00.160
Hey, Hase.

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:02.000
What I was saying before...

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:04.300
Oh? Just forget that dream.

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:07.160
No, not that dream.

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:09.760
It's a real thing that seems like a dream.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:13.780
I went back to the apartment, right?

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:15.980
That's great.

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:19.230
You feel a lot more relaxed than before.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:23.320
I'm sure that must be a 
place where you can relax.

00:18:23.320 --> 00:18:24.350
Yeah.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:25.920
<i>That's right.</i>

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:29.310
<i>The apartment is like a dream for me.</i>

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:32.830
<i>So I want you to see it, too.</i>

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:35.040
Hase?

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:39.880
What are you looking at?

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:41.380
You wanna fight, kid?

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:42.660
You're in the way.

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:43.420
Move.

00:18:44.150 --> 00:18:46.950
Don't tell us what to do, kid.

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:51.120
They told you at school to 
respect your superiors, right?

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:53.430
Superiors?

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:56.580
By superiors, do you mean you?

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.340
Of course, damn it!

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:04.230
I refuse to accept someone as an adult 
simply because they've gotten older.

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:07.430
Let's go, Inaba.

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:08.330
Yeah.

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:11.950
Hey, asshole!

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:18.990
Idiots.

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:20.990
That's what happens when
you pick a fight with Hase.

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:27.690
Wait, damn it!

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:29.660
You'll pay, you damn kids!

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:31.780
They chased us?

00:19:32.930 --> 00:19:34.210
What a pain.

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:35.520
Let's run!

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:43.070
What is this place?

00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:44.720
A construction site?

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:46.530
A dead end, huh?

00:19:48.690 --> 00:19:50.330
They're here already.

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:51.650
Over there.

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:58.560
Inaba, you seal the exit.

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:02.960
You're a 4th-degree black belt in aikido.
One hit and they'll get scared, right?

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:05.100
If they've got any brains 
to get scared with, sure.

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:07.240
What do you mean?

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:09.150
Even brawls have rules.

00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:13.480
Usually it's over when both sides 
see how good the other is.

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:17.720
But lately, it's all people 
who've never been in a fight.

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:21.950
So they can't hold back when 
it comes to pain and fear.

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:25.870
What could have been resolved with one punch
ends with them beating someone to death.

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:28.930
It's especially that way 
for people in gangs.

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:32.610
The word "mass hysteria" exists because nobody
knows what people in a group might do.

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:35.300
Seriously?

00:20:35.990 --> 00:20:39.170
Come out, brats!

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:40.840
Fine...

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:42.080
Be ready.

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:47.760
You seem to be in trouble.

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:49.570
I sure am.

00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:53.450
What a pleasant afternoon, master.

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:56.540
Huh?

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:57.610
Fool?

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:59.660
I'm not dreaming now, am I?

00:20:59.660 --> 00:21:02.540
It's no dream, master!

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:07.670
You released us from our seal last night
and made us your servants!

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:09.680
It wasn't a dream?

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:13.450
And you mean I'm the master 
of all those useless spirits?

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:16.020
Useless, eh? Harsh!

00:21:16.020 --> 00:21:18.930
Well, some of them can 
be rather lazy, but...

00:21:18.930 --> 00:21:21.640
They were totally useless.

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:24.600
A blind old man? A 500 yen genie?

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:25.870
Inaba...

00:21:25.870 --> 00:21:27.680
Shut up! I'm busy.

00:21:31.210 --> 00:21:33.440
What is that?

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:36.680
Hase...

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:38.680
To be continued in the next episode!

00:23:11.400 --> 00:23:12.840
What do I do? What do I do?

00:23:12.840 --> 00:23:15.080
Those thugs are seriously mad!

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:18.490
Forget that. What's this weird Fool thing?

00:23:18.490 --> 00:23:22.990
Wah-wah! They're almost here! 
We're in terrible danger!

00:23:22.990 --> 00:23:25.170
You're doing that deliberately, aren't you?

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:26.460
You saw through it, huh?

00:23:26.990 --> 00:23:31.550
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:
"I'm in Training."

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:31.550
<b>Seventh Haunting
I'm in Training</b>

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:34.270
Inaba, don't hide things from me.

00:23:34.270 --> 00:23:34.850
Hase...
